import json
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
report=json.loads((p/'results.json').read_text())
# Exact calculations are Python Decimal. The page only formats stored results.
doc='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><style>
body{margin:0;font-family:var(--font-sans,system-ui);color:var(--foreground,#20252b);font-size:15px}p{line-height:1.5;margin:8px 0 16px}.muted,small{color:var(--muted-foreground,#68727c)}.controls{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:16px 0}label{flex:1;min-width:200px;font-size:13px}select{display:block;margin-top:7px;padding:9px;width:100%;color:inherit;background:var(--secondary,#edf1f3);border:1px solid var(--border,#bbb);border-radius:6px;font:inherit}.presets{display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:16px}button{font:inherit;color:inherit;cursor:pointer;border:1px solid var(--border,#aaa);border-radius:6px;background:var(--secondary,#edf1f3);padding:7px 10px}.presets button{font-size:12px}table{border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:5px;width:100%;table-layout:fixed}th{font-size:12px;font-weight:500;padding:4px 0}th:first-child{width:64px;text-align:left}td{padding:0}td button{width:100%;min-height:46px;border:2px solid transparent;border-radius:7px;font-weight:650;font-size:16px;padding:4px 0}td button[aria-pressed="true"]{border-color:var(--foreground,#222);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px var(--background,#fff)}.stats{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:18px 0}.stat{flex:1;min-width:135px;padding:16px;border-radius:var(--radius,8px);background:var(--secondary,#eef2f4);font-size:13px}.stat strong{display:block;font-size:25px;margin:7px 0}.note{font-size:13px;line-height:1.5}details{margin:16px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:13px}#selection{margin:16px 0 0}#distribution{padding-left:12px;border-left:3px solid #408dba}a{color:var(--accent,#2486b4)}@media(max-width:430px){table{border-spacing:3px}td button{font-size:14px}th:first-child{width:53px}.stat{min-width:115px}}
</style></head><body>
<p><b>Price × fee growth: how much of the incentive remains?</b><br>Conditional replay of 100 pools from M2’s October 9 snapshot. Each pool acts independently under proposed October MFS rules. Fee scenarios stay at or above baseline.</p>
<div class="controls"><label>Where additional customer fees go<select id="mode"><option value="proportional">Follow existing fee shares</option><option value="stake_proportional_additions">New fees spread by stake share</option></select></label><label>What the matrix measures<select id="metric"><option value="profitable_pools">Pools with any positive opportunity</option><option value="above_10_pools">Pools with opportunity above $10</option><option value="median_peak_all_100">Median maximum gain, all 100 pools</option></select></label></div>
<div class="presets"><button data-h="1" data-g="1">Baseline</button><button data-h="1.5" data-g="1">Price +50%</button><button data-h="2" data-g="1">Price +100%</button><button data-h="2" data-g="2">Both +100%</button><button data-h="1" data-g="2">Fees +100%</button></div>
<p class="note muted" id="matrixLabel"></p><table aria-label="Price and fee sensitivity"><thead><tr><th>LPT price ↓<br>Fees →</th>__HEAD__</tr></thead><tbody id="matrix"></tbody></table>
<p id="selection"></p><div class="stats"><div class="stat">Any profitable action<strong id="count"></strong><span id="stake"></span></div><div class="stat">Potential above $10<strong id="above"></strong><span>Per pool, for this round</span></div><div class="stat">Median maximum gain<strong id="median"></strong><span>All 100 pools, including zeros</span></div></div>
<p id="comparison"></p><p class="note" id="distribution"></p>
<details><summary>Model assumptions and reproducibility</summary><p class="note">Baseline: round 4364; $820.960664 of indexed fees replayed as USDC; LPT valuation $1.71765; scheduled ceiling 29,288.551807 LPT calibrated at hypothetical launch r=0. Node allocation 94%; operator-side fee split 50%; unchanged scores of 1. Stake, commissions and capture-time operator-address ownership proxies stay fixed. Real work is invoiced at $1 per unit with $0.30 execution cost. No setup cost, financing, cash limit, capacity limit, opportunity cost, price feedback or organizational ownership consolidation. Added fees represent hypothetical external demand; recorded baseline settlements do not prove independent demand. Traffic is represented through paid fees, not a measured job-count forecast.</p><p class="note">The median is the middle of the 100 individually optimized gains, counting zero when no action pays. These are separate opportunities, not simultaneous actions; they must not be summed as a network attack. LPT gains are valued unsold tokens, not realized cash. Decimal calculations checked all 5,000 selected optima against the M2 accounting engine, reconciled the earlier 100-pool baseline and checked equal-growth scaling for 300 pool/scenario pairs. Exploratory analysis, not an accepted milestone result or observed misconduct.</p></details>
<script>const D=__DATA__, $=id=>document.getElementById(id);let h='1',g='1';const lookup=(mode,p,f)=>D.scenarios.find(s=>s.mode===mode&&s.price_factor===p&&s.fee_factor===f),money=n=>'$'+Number(n).toFixed(2);function draw(){const mode=$('mode').value,key=$('metric').value,base=lookup(mode,'1','1'),picked=lookup(mode,h,g);$('matrixLabel').textContent=key==='median_peak_all_100'?'Cells show USDC-equivalent gain per round. Darker cells mean larger gains. Click a cell to inspect it.':'Cells show counts out of 100 pools. Darker cells mean more pools qualify. Click a cell to inspect it.';
const max=Math.max(...D.scenarios.filter(s=>s.mode===mode).map(s=>Number(s[key])));$('matrix').innerHTML=D.price_factors.map(p=>'<tr><th scope="row">'+p+'×</th>'+D.fee_factors.map(f=>{let s=lookup(mode,p,f),v=Number(s[key]),alpha=.07+.48*v/max;return`<td><button data-h="${p}" data-g="${f}" aria-label="Price ${p} times, fees ${f} times: ${key==='median_peak_all_100'?money(v):v}" aria-pressed="${p===h&&f===g}" style="background:rgba(55,143,190,${alpha})">${key==='median_peak_all_100'?money(v):v}</button></td>`}).join('')+'</tr>').join('');
$('selection').innerHTML=`<b>Selected: LPT value ${h}× · total fees ${g}×</b><br><small>${money(picked.price_usdc_per_lpt)}/LPT · ${money(picked.fees_usdc)} of fees in the round</small>`;$('count').textContent=picked.profitable_pools+' / 100';$('stake').textContent=(100*Number(picked.profitable_stake_share)).toFixed(1)+'% of modeled stake';$('above').textContent=picked.above_10_pools+' / 100';$('median').textContent=money(picked.median_peak_all_100);
let factor=Number(h)/Number(g);$('comparison').textContent=mode==='proportional'?`Reward value per dollar of network fees is ${factor.toFixed(2)}× baseline. With unchanged fee shares, this scales every below-cap pool’s initial reward-to-cost incentive by the same factor. ${h===g&&h!=='1'?'The same pools qualify, while each pool’s optimal spending and maximum gain scale by '+h+'×.':''}`:`Reward value per dollar of network fees is ${factor.toFixed(2)}× baseline. This allocation also moves fee shares toward stake shares, consuming unused reward headroom. The network-wide ratio alone cannot describe the resulting gain.`;
$('distribution').textContent=mode==='proportional'?'Existing business grows proportionally: every pool retains its previous fee share. Pools with zero baseline fees receive none of the new fees. This isolates the price-versus-total-fees effect.':'Only new fees are allocated in proportion to stake. Existing fees stay where they were. Pools with little previous business receive new business. This is a diagnostic comparison of fee distribution, not a proposed routing rule or a forecast.';
}
document.body.addEventListener('click',e=>{let b=e.target.closest('button[data-h]');if(b){h=b.dataset.h;g=b.dataset.g;draw()}});$('mode').onchange=draw;$('metric').onchange=draw;
console.assert(lookup('proportional','1','1').profitable_pools===79,'Baseline count');console.assert(lookup('proportional','1.5','1').profitable_pools===81,'Price sensitivity');console.assert(Math.abs(Number(lookup('proportional','2','2').median_peak_all_100)-2*Number(lookup('proportional','1','1').median_peak_all_100))<1e-8,'Equal-growth median');console.assert(D.scenarios.length===50,'Scenario matrix complete');draw();document.querySelector('.presets button[data-h="2"][data-g="2"]').click();console.assert($('count').textContent==='79 / 100'&&$('median').textContent==='$30.30','Preset updates results');$('mode').value='stake_proportional_additions';$('mode').dispatchEvent(new Event('change'));console.assert($('median').textContent==='$15.15','Allocation control updates results');$('metric').value='above_10_pools';$('metric').dispatchEvent(new Event('change'));console.assert(document.querySelector('#matrix button[aria-pressed="true"]').textContent==='60','Matrix metric control updates');$('mode').value='proportional';$('metric').value='profitable_pools';document.querySelector('.presets button[data-h="1"][data-g="1"]').click();console.log('PASS: numeric anchors, 50 scenarios, preset, allocation and metric interactions');
</script></body></html>'''
doc=doc.replace('__HEAD__',''.join('<th scope="col">'+g+'×</th>' for g in report['fee_factors'])).replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(report))
(p/'growth.html').write_text(doc)
print(p/'growth.html')
